erning an observer’s capacity to integrate records over time. Classicality becomes a decomposition-indexed property, not a global feature of the universal wavefunction. Applied to Wigner’s Friend and Frauchiger–Renner, the framework dissolves paradoxes by showing that cross-agent inferences fail precisely in regimes where effective accessibility is low. The paper outlines experimental signatures, including observer-dependent classicality thresholds and flow-disruption tests, offering a route toward empirical constraints on observer-relative quantum structure."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W7161705706", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20289213", "title": "Finite Record Boundaries in Wigner's Friend Scenarios: Observer-Relative Distinguishability and Quantum Record Availability in Finite Distinction Systems", "publication_year": 2026, "type": "article", "cited_by_coun

